From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:19:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Reconnect Trouter with a backoff and survive empty responses

The consumer Trouter websocket can close or error right after it opens.
The handler then reconnected at once; each retry tended to get an empty
trouter-info body, json_decode_object() returned NULL, and the code went
on to ref and read members of that NULL. The result was a tight reconnect
loop, a flood of json-glib criticals, and an account that stopped sending
after some minutes.

- Reconnect on a doubling backoff (5 s up to 300 s), reset once the
  websocket opens, and cancel a pending reconnect in teams_trouter_stop().
- Bail out (and back off) when the trouter-info response does not decode.
- Skip 3: and 5: frames whose request or body do not decode, and frames
  without a "headers" object, instead of dereferencing NULL.
- Only walk "connectparams" when it is present, in the info, sessionid
  and authenticate paths.
- Bound the index 0/1 accesses on "files", "Groups" and thread "members"
  arrays, which can be absent or short, and only unref "files" when set.
- Log why the Skype contact roster came back empty.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
